.TH SDL_utf8strnlen 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_utf8strnlen \- Count the number of codepoints in a UTF-8 string, up to n bytes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_utf8strnlen(const char *str, size_t bytes);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts the _codepoints_, not _bytes_, in
.BR str ,
excluding the null terminator\[char46]
.PP
If you need to count the bytes in a string instead, consider using
.BR SDL_strnlen ()\[char46]
.PP
The counting stops at
.BR bytes
bytes (not codepoints!)\[char46] This seems counterintuitive, but makes it easy to express the total size of the string\(aqs buffer\[char46]
.PP
Since this handles Unicode, it expects the strings to be well-formed UTF-8 and not a null-terminated string of arbitrary bytes\[char46] Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 are treated as Unicode character U+FFFD (REPLACEMENT CHARACTER), so a malformed or incomplete UTF-8 sequence might increase the count by several replacement characters\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I str
The null-terminated UTF-8 string to read\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I bytes
The maximum amount of bytes to count\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns The length (in codepoints, excluding the null terminator) of
.BR src
but never more than
.BR maxlen \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_utf8strlen (3),
